# Handoff — 2026-08-10: NEW-AGENT TEST — verify MCP door + audit trace (D-128) via the IN-CHAT tool surface

## Your job (fresh agent, fresh conversation)

Test the agentide MCP door and the D-128 audit fix **using the in-chat MCP tools** — NOT curl, NOT scripts. This conversation could not because its tool schema lacked the MCP tools (D-127 client-provisioning: tools are provisioned at conversation creation; restarts don't re-inject them into an EXISTING chat). **You must be in a NEW conversation** so `product_list` / `session_list` etc. are in your callable set.

## What is running RIGHT NOW (verify with `ss -tln`)

- Gateway (local bundle, ALL fixes D-123..128): ports **7100 (MCP) + 7350 (SDK) + 7300/7200/7400**
- Example app: **:3000**, 11 business caps registered
- Token: `/tmp/ag-mcp.token` (1h TTL — if expired: `agentide token issue --tenant acme --caller zed --scope '*' --data-dir /tmp/ag-mcp | tail -1 > /tmp/ag-mcp.token`)
- Data dir: `/tmp/ag-mcp` — **audit log at `/tmp/ag-mcp/audit.log`**

If the gateway is down: `setsid node /home/spanexx/Shared/Learn/Agent-Bridge-SDK/agentide/packages/agentide/dist/bin.bundled.cjs gateway start --data-dir /tmp/ag-mcp --all-doors --foreground > /tmp/gw-fg.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &` (boot from the agentide repo dir). App: `cd /home/spanexx/Shared/Learn/Agent-Bridge-SDK/example && node dist/main.js` (boot from ITS dir — .env is cwd-relative).

## The TEST (4 steps)

1. **Wipe the audit baseline** (terminal is fine for this):
   `rm -f /tmp/ag-mcp/audit.log` → `wc -l /tmp/ag-mcp/audit.log` → 0 (or missing file)

2. **Call the business tool IN-CHAT** (the whole point — no curl):
   - `product_list` → expect 28 real items (HAM-9 Hammer, SKU-001 Widget…), NO session params needed (D-126 auto-mint)
   - `cart_add` → expect totalCents (write path)

3. **Check the audit log** (terminal):
   `wc -l /tmp/ag-mcp/audit.log` → expect **8 rows** for the 2 calls:
   ```
   session.create  ok     (auto-mint)
   product.list    denied (first attempt, no session)
   product.list    ok     (retry with session)
   session.destroy ok     (cleanup)
   ← same 4 for cart_add
   ```
   Full command: `grep -oE '"name":"[a-z.]*"|"status":"[a-z]*"' /tmp/ag-mcp/audit.log | paste - - | sort | uniq -c`

4. **PASS criteria**: tools callable in-chat, business data returned, audit log accumulates the full lifecycle (create → denied → ok → destroy) per call, in order. That = D-123..128 verified end-to-end through the REAL surface.

## Why this matters

- D-128 (Critical, commit `cc49119`): the audit log previously held ≤1 row (CLI fs truncated instead of appending). The fix (reuse `nodeFileSystem()`) is committed + pushed but only verified over the WIRE so far (8 rows for 2 curls). The in-chat call + audit check is the missing end-to-end proof.
- User principle: **everything must be logged and traceable.**

## If a step fails

- Tool not in schema → you're in the WRONG conversation (must be NEW). Do NOT fall back to curl — report it.
- Audit rows missing/1 row → the fix regressed or the gateway runs a STALE bundle (rebuild chain: edit src → `npx tsc -b` in the package → `pnpm run bundle` in packages/agentide → restart gateway by PID from `ss -ltnp`).
- `GATEWAY_AUTH_FAILED` → token expired → re-mint (above).

## User-only follow-ups

- After PASS: the release (0.9.4 rides D-123..128) — ask the user if they want `release-agentide`.
- The D-127 client-refresh (tools appearing without restarts) is the known external follow-up — do NOT try to fix it here.

